Scenarios

Scenario A: Shard 0 outage

Hypothesis: Shards 1-3 track normally; shard-0 campaigns `503 shard_unavailable`; unknown IDs in stale-serve `503 registry_stale`; outbox stays PENDING; budget invariant on shards 1-3.

CI: `tests/resilience/shard_outage_fault_test.go`. Drill: `scripts/fault/shard0_outage_drill.sh`.

Steps: baseline traffic -> stop `redis-0` -> verify breaker, latency on 1-3, outbox PENDING -> restart -> breaker closes, outbox flushes, `AssertBudgetInvariant`.

Proof: `fault_proof fault=shard_0_outage status=recovered`, `fault_proof fault=shard0_survival_shards_1_3`.

Scenario A2: Local quanta graceful shutdown

Hypothesis: Unused RAM quanta return to Redis `budget:quota` on SIGTERM/FlushAll; recon tolerance holds.

Proof: `fault_proof fault=local_quota_flush`.

Scenario B: Single Redis master outage (non-shard-0)

Hypothesis: ~1/N campaigns affected; unaffected shards within latency budget; breaker opens and closes on recovery.

Scenario C: Postgres primary unavailable

Hypothesis: Processor pauses stream ack; outbox PENDING; no duplicate ledger rows; recovery drains backlog.

Scenario D: ClickHouse write stall

Hypothesis: CH gate backpressure; mmap spool absorbs; no unbounded memory; lag decreases after CH restore.

Multi-region (M7)

Catalog: `docs/MULTI_REGION.md` §13. Minimum proofs: `RESILIENCE_MIN_PROOFS_MR=12`.

CH-MR-01 (New node during `NODE_WARMUP_SEC`): weight capped; `provenance=neighbor_median`
CH-MR-02 (Scrape blackhole 3 epochs): no drain without hard signal; neighbor fallback
CH-MR-03 (All neighbors unhealthy): `historical_daily`; gentle drain only
CH-MR-04 (Disk fsync latency +5 ms): `disk_degraded`; proxy shed; tracker p99 stable
CH-MR-05 (KeyGen CPU throttle): ingress shed; single D3 proposal per `op_id`
CH-MR-06 (Executor PG partition): lease `expired`; retry; `AssertBudgetInvariant`
CH-MR-07 (Ghost executor): `already_confirmed`; no double Redis write
CH-MR-08 (Dual CAS `executing`): one PG winner only
CH-MR-09 (Quorum book 1-of-3): no client ACK until 2-of-3
CH-MR-10 (Global PG partition 60 s): hot path OK; proxy WAL spool; heal drains
CH-MR-11 (UDP epoch loss): equal weights; no aggressive drain
CH-MR-12 (Drain 3 epochs): weight → 0; in-flight completes

Proof format:

```text
fault_proof fault=mr_<name> <key>=<value> baseline_ok=true
```

